From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] grt: free the blocked intervals once they are applied
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

findObstructions, findInstancesObstructions and findNetsObstructions
collect, per partly blocked edge and layer, the intervals obstructions
block; initBlockedIntervals turns them into capacity adjustments. Nothing
reads them after that: a release recomputes from the capacity, and the
next initialization starts from clear(). They were kept to the end of
the run, an interval set per edge, on a large die several GB.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
index cc40411075..57570c6ab9 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
@@ -1035,6 +1035,11 @@ void FastRouteCore::initBlockedIntervals(std::vector<int>& track_space)
       addAdjustment(x, y, x + 1, y, layer, edge_cap, true);
     }
   }
+
+  // The intervals are applied as the adjustments above and read nowhere
+  // else; on a large die they hold an interval set per blocked edge.
+  decltype(vertical_blocked_intervals_)().swap(vertical_blocked_intervals_);
+  decltype(horizontal_blocked_intervals_)().swap(horizontal_blocked_intervals_);
 }
 
 int FastRouteCore::getAvailableResources(int x1,
